Event When it runs <code>setup(frm)</code> Once per form load — <code>set_query</code> goes here <code>onload(frm)</code> When the form loads (after setup) <code>refresh(frm)</code> Every time the form re-renders — buttons and visibility go here <code>fieldname(frm)</code> When one field changes (for example <code>purpose(frm)</code>) <code>validate(frm)</code> Before save — UX hint only, never the real check <code>after_save(frm)</code> After a successful save <p>Child table rows get their own block, in the parent's file:</p> <pre><code>frappe.ui.form.on("Gate Pass Item", {
    qty(frm, cdt, cdn) {
        const row = locals[cdt][cdn];
        if (row.qty &lt;= 0) {
            frappe.msgprint(__("Row {0}: Qty must be greater than 0", [row.idx]));
        }
    },
    items_remove(frm) {
        frappe.show_alert({ message: __("Item removed"), indicator: "orange" }, 3);
    },
});
</code></pre>
